Subject: Make JavaScript source parsing an optional build capability

Base: rusty_v8 v0.106.0, V8 12.9.202.13. Applies after no-regexp.patch.

v8_enable_javascript_parser defaults to true, preserving the upstream source
implementations and build. The custom_wee8 toolchain scope opts out. A separate GN target
implements the parsing interface by reporting an explicit compilation error;
the parser, preparser, scanner, text streams, literal buffer, rewriter and
name inferrer are excluded from
that build. The shared compiler guards its direct background-parser invocation.

This removes JavaScript source parsing, not all JavaScript runtime machinery.
Wasm compilation, builtin generation, context creation and native wrappers
remain. AST metadata is still shared with the compiler. No Wasm text parser is added; wee8 consumes Wasm binary modules.

On upgrade, check direct Parser/PreParser callers, the parsing interface,
background compilation, snapshot generation and the GN exclusion list. Validate
both ordinary and custom targets, rejection of source APIs, Wasm instantiation and GC.

